	(text "Pixel PCB (one per house). 12 V, WS2814F driver, 3 x RGBW 5050 LEDs, 3 per channel in series.
Chain in on J1 (male), out on J2 (female). Servo pinout: 1 = data, 2 = +12 V, 3 = GND.
Reversed plug: GND and data swap. The house's local ground then returns through the upstream DOUT
and through our DIN pin. R2 + D1 carry that current around the WS2814 input.
Offset plug (one pin over): 12 V can land on DATA_IN. R2 limits the current into VDD through D1.
R4 moves ~2 V of the red channel's excess headroom off the WS2814 (red Vf 1.8-2.4 V x3).
WS2814F data order is W,R,G,B (datasheet p.4); set the color order in WLED to match.
TBD: R2 value, whether D1 is needed, R4 value, custom footprints for U1 and D2-D4."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 160.02 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "c1520f0d-422a-59d6-a31d-1d89dec1df87")
	)
